; S:Startup-Sequence for an ENiGMA½ Amiga door image.
;
; Boots straight into the host shim, which owns the serial port, says hello and
; ready to ENiGMA, then runs whichever door each session names (BBS:Doors/...).
; Doors look for the BBS under BBS:, so BBS: is the boot volume.  A minimal image
; has no C:Assign; axshim then makes BBS: (SYS:) and DOORS: (SYS:Doors) itself.
; Nothing after C:axshim runs: it never returns while the machine is up.
FailAt 21
Stack 32768
If EXISTS C:Assign
    C:Assign >NIL: BBS: SYS:
    C:Assign >NIL: DOORS: SYS:Doors
EndIf
C:axshim 115200
